  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Largest federal contracts by total value, FY2027 to date lists the biggest single-contract relationships measured by full contract value rather than annual obligations. NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC tops the ranking at $44.1B. UT-BATTELLE LLC follows at $43B and LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC appears third at $42.2B. The list includes multiple national laboratory operators and major defense contractors, with TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC at $36.3B, CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC at $35.2B, and BATTELLE MEMORIAL INSTITUTE at $31.2B. SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC and BATTELLE ENERGY ALLIANCE, LLC report $28B and $26.8B respectively. THE BOEING COMPANY and THE REGENTS OF THE UNIVERSITY OF CALIFORNIA round out the top ten at $22.7B and $20.2B. The report period is FY2027 to date. Note. Total award value figures are full contract values, not single-year obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which organizations top the FY2027 list?",
        "body": "NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC leads the list with $44.1B. UT-BATTELLE LLC and LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC follow at $43B and $42.2B. TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC, CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC, and BATTELLE MEMORIAL INSTITUTE also appear in the top six with $36.3B, $35.2B, and $31.2B respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What other large contract holders appear in the top ten?",
        "body": "SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC and BATTELLE ENERGY ALLIANCE, LLC report $28B and $26.8B. THE BOEING COMPANY and THE REGENTS OF THE UNIVERSITY OF CALIFORNIA complete the top ten at $22.7B and $20.2B. The list emphasizes long-term, high-value contracts across national laboratory management and defense industry partners."
      }
    ]
